 "sentences": [
  "Failure is an accepted part of the process, as long as we learn from our mistakes and use those lessons to improve.",
  "When it comes to your coding practices, I want you to always start your function names with 'gn_'.",
  "This is a convention we follow in our team to easily identify our custom functions.",
  "We'll be covering various aspects of our coding standards and best practices as you go along.",
  "For now, focus on getting familiar with our core development practices and don't hesitate to ask questions.",
  "We're here to support you and make sure you have everything you need to succeed.",
  "Precisely.",
  "Additionally, I want to emphasize code sharing, so we should integrate a code snippet feature with syntax highlighting and the ability to comment and collaborate on code.",
  "Now, as you begin development, I want you to keep code maintainability and readability in mind.",
  "We should establish clear coding standards and guidelines for the project, and I have a few specific instructions for you to follow.",
  "For function argument names, always include a single digit and ensure that the name starts with 'e_'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency and make our code easier to understand and collaborate on.",
  "Not for now.",
  "Just ensure that you consistently apply this naming convention for function arguments.",
  "It's crucial for maintaining clean and understandable code, especially as this project will likely involve contributions from multiple team members.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or need any assistance along the way.",
  "Keep me updated on your progress, and feel free to stop by if you encounter any challenges or simply want to discuss your ideas.",
  "My door is always open."
 ],
